  m_Name: ecs
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: GameTerms.Runtime::GameTerms.GlossaryTermAsset
  data:
    Id: ecs
    Term: Entity Component System
    Abbreviation: ecs
    Category: 1
    Difficulty: 2
    ShortDefinition: An architecture where gameplay data lives in components and
      behavior runs in systems over entities.
    SimpleExplanation: Store traits in small data chunks and let systems process
      matching groups efficiently.
    WhyItMatters: ECS can improve performance and scale for large numbers of similar
      game objects.
    Example: A movement system updates every entity that has position and velocity
      components.
    CommonMistake: Stuffing unrelated data into one giant component and losing the
      data-oriented benefit.
    PracticePrompt: Model a projectile as separate transform, velocity, and lifetime
      components.
    GameUses:
    - Large-scale simulation
    - Performance-critical gameplay
    - Data-oriented design
    RelatedTermIds:
    - dependency-injection
    - object-pooling
    - data-oriented-design
    Tags:
    - architecture
    - performance
    - data
    Synonyms:
    - ecs
